From c174b2d69cef7f9d374577f151330e45df1163eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:25:26 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 download history at scale: sliced history loads, a
 live-item limit and archived rows for the host

A profile's download history loaded in one UI task: DownloadHistory made a
DownloadItem for every History DB row, and every item's observers ran, at
the session's first download. With 39,413 rows that task took ~0.5 s and
footprint grew ~250 MB, then the bridge replayed every item to the host.

DownloadHistory now hands the rows to a worker, which still decides the
rows to forget (overwritten files) in database order, orders the rest
newest first and applies the profile's live limit. The UI thread creates
the items in slices of 8 ms, newest first, and the rows are freed on a
worker. With a live limit (DownloadHistory::SetLoadPolicy) only the newest
N complete rows become items, with every unfinished row, every row the
in-progress DB holds and every row without a URL; older complete rows stay
in the database as immutable archived rows. Clearing download history
(ChromeBrowsingDataRemoverDelegate) deletes matching archived rows too.

ABI 1.48 (download_history, bridge 0.50.0): ReArcDownloadSetHistoryPolicy,
ReArcDownloadLoadHistory, ReArcEngineSetDownloadHistoryCallback,
ReArcDownloadGetHistoryInfo, ReArcDownloadQueryArchived (pages copied on a
worker, posted on main), ReArcDownloadRemoveArchived and
ReArcDownloadGetTimes (restored items keep their own dates; the download
event carries none). framework.exports and framework.order list the seven
functions. Existing ABI layouts remain unchanged.

Last rebased: 2026-11-07 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
